SUMMARY:"Vengeance Like This": Expressing and Instigating Rage in Hebrew 
 Poetry
DESCRIPTION:Join the Program in Judaic Studies for a seminar with Vered K
 arti Shemtov on Monday\, September 28. This talk explores the aesthetics
 \, evolution\, and political co-optation of rage in modern Hebrew poetry
 \, focusing on Hayim Nahman Bialik’s 1906 trilogy From the Poetry of R
 age (Mi-shirei ha-Za’am). By examining the sequence of “On the Slaug
 hter” (1903)\, “In the City of Slaughter” (1903)\, and “I Knew i
 n a Night of Fog” (1905)\, the presentation demonstrates how Bialik’
 s poetic rage evolves from an immediate visceral outcry and internal mor
 al critique following the Kishinev pogrom into a transformat\nhttps://ww
 w.princeton.edu/events/2026/vengeance-expressing-and-instigating-rage-he
 brew-poetry
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/vengeance-expressing-and-instig
 ating-rage-hebrew-poetry
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
