SUMMARY:Tour of Marquand Library
LOCATION:Marquand Art Library\, Marquand Art Library
DESCRIPTION:Marquand Library\, founded in 1908\, is one of the finest art
  libraries in North America. Marquand re-opened within the new Art Museu
 m complex after an almost five-year hiatus in January 2026. Tours of the
  five-floor non-circulating library will be led by Rebecca Friedman\, Ar
 t Librarian for Research Services\, who has worked at Marquand since 200
 7. Be our guest where you'll learn more about the building\, its feature
 s and collections. At this time\, tours of Marquand Library are limited 
 to those with a Princeton University ID card but arrangements can be mad
 e for others by request. The group will meet in the lobby outside Marqua
 nd Library\, which can be accessed via the walkway from McCosh Walk dire
 ctly across from Murray-Dodge Hall and parallel to the main Museum entra
 nce down the stairs (to the LEFT).\nAudience: Faculty & Academic Profess
 ionals\, Staff\, Students\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/tour-ma
 rquand-library-3
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/tour-marquand-library-3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
