SUMMARY:Talk: Elizabeth Oyler
DESCRIPTION:This lecture explores Furukawa Hideo’s 2016 translation of 
 the Japanese literary classic\, "The Tale of the Heike." A narrative rec
 ounting Japan’s Genpei Civil War (1180–85)\, "The Tale of the Heike"
  has influenced Japanese culture since its first compilation in the earl
 y fourteenth century. In a talk titled “Furukawa Hideo’s post-3/11 H
 eike monogatari\,” Elizabeth Oyler\, author and associate professor of
  Japanese at the University of Pittsburgh\, examines the ways in which t
 he tale has been adapted in response to contemporary events. Introduced 
 by Kit Brooks\, the Museum’s curator of Asian art. Th\nhttps://www.pri
 nceton.edu/events/2026/talk-elizabeth-oyler
