SUMMARY:Earth Shed Exhibition Opening
DESCRIPTION:Earth Shed Exhibition designed and organized by Assistant Pro
 fessor of Architecture Erin Besler | Besler & Sons Earth Shed is an inst
 allation and distributed building practice that begins with the construc
 tion site and its contents. It’s made primarily from soil sourced from
  the project site\, rammed and compacted into earth blocks. The project 
 conceives the construction site as a platform for experiential learning 
 and research\, focusing attention on the ordinary tasks of building and 
 how they organize people\, materials\, skills\, and knowledge across con
 texts. A series of workshops invites parti\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/ev
 ents/2026/earth-shed-exhibition-opening
