SUMMARY:Glee Club Presents: Christ Church (Oxford) Cathedral Choir
LOCATION:Princeton University Chapel
DESCRIPTION:As part of this year’s ‘Glee Club Presents’ series\, Th
 e Christ Church Cathedral Choir celebrates its 500th anniversary and per
 forms in collaboration with the students of the Glee Club. This program 
 showcases the rich musical legacy of a unique foundation — one that is
  both Oxford’s cathedral and a college of the University of Oxford. Th
 e program traces that history from John Taverner\, appointed by Cardinal
  Wolsey in 1526 as the first Informator Choristarum\, to more recently a
 ssociated composers. A newly commissioned cantata by Composer in Residen
 ce Nico Muhly explores how poetry\, art\, and glass act as a membrane be
 tween the visible world and the divine. Tickets Free\, Unticketed About 
 Christ Church Cathedral Choir King Henry VIII established the Collegiate
  Foundation in 1546\, including one Organist and eight Lay Clerks\, plus
  provision for a schoolmaster to educate the choristers. In the l\nAudie
 nce: Open to the Public\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/glee-club
 -presents-christ-church-oxford-cathedral-choir
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/glee-club-presents-christ-churc
 h-oxford-cathedral-choir
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
