SUMMARY:Library Research for Water Chemistry
LOCATION:Commons Large\, Hybrid Meeting Room (D312)\, Commons Library
DESCRIPTION:The Princeton University Library provides print and digital l
 ibrary sources from chemistry and geosciences collections specific to ch
 emical and geologic processes. This 30-minute introductory workshop will
  provide attendees with tips to finding library research for water chemi
 stry\, aqueous mining industries\, and intersections with technology. Fr
 om 2008 to 2018\, Emily was the research librarian for the USGS chemistr
 y and geology laboratories https://www.usgs.gov/science/laboratories Emi
 ly’s Library Research Guides: Chemistry https://libguides.princeton.ed
 u/chem Geosciences https://libguides.princeton.edu/geo\nAudience: Facult
 y & Academic Professionals\, Staff\, Students\nhttps://www.princeton.edu
 /events/2026/library-research-water-chemistry
