SUMMARY:Program in the Ancient World - Michael Nylan Talk
DESCRIPTION:It is far from easy to do either cross-chronological or cross
 -cultural history well. As someone engaged for nearly forty years in for
 ging comparisons of both types\, I have experienced the promise and peri
 ls\, as well as the blank walls. Far too few historians think about what
  topics are truly comparable\; at the same time\, the minute we think or
  write or talk about another era or another culture in English\, we are 
 doing comparative history\, and to pretend otherwise is likely to spur a
 historical imaginaries. This talk will try to summarize what comparative
  approaches generally work and where the \nhttps://www.princeton.edu/eve
 nts/2026/program-ancient-world-michael-nylan-talk
