 ion\, joins the orchestra as soloist for Korngold's lush\, cinematic Cel
 lo Concerto. The program closes with Dvořák's Symphony No. 8 in G majo
 r\, a work celebrated for its warmth\, lyricism\, and folk-inflected mel
 odies. Conducted by Michael Pratt\, Professor of the Practice\, Director
