SUMMARY:Musicology Colloquium with Benjamin Barson
DESCRIPTION:The Musicology Colloquium presents a talk by Benjamin Barson.
 AbstractThis talk introduces new research from my current book project\,
  "Jazz Against Fascism\," which traces how musicians\, dockworkers\, bro
 adcasters\, and anti-imperialist organizers transformed popular African 
 American-derived music into a medium of solidarity across the circum-Car
 ibbean world. Building from my first book\, Brassroots Democracy\, the t
 alk follows brass bands\, dance orchestras\, radio infrastructures\, lab
 or movements\, and Black internationalist networks linking New Orleans\,
  Cuba\, Haiti\, Mexico\, and the wider Caribbean u\nhttps://www.princeto
 n.edu/events/2026/musicology-colloquium-benjamin-barson
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/musicology-colloquium-benjamin-
 barson
